    <h2><span data-i18n="review.common.frequently.asked.questions">Frequently Asked Questions</span></h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is Butterfly iQ FDA approved for clinical use?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Butterfly iQ has FDA 510(k) clearance for 13 clinical applications including abdominal, cardiac, OB/GYN, musculoskeletal, thoracic, vascular, urological, and pediatric imaging. It meets rigorous safety and efficacy standards for diagnostic use in clinical settings. The device is also CE marked for use in Europe and approved in many other countries worldwide.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What is the image quality compared to traditional ultrasound?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Butterfly iQ provides diagnostic-quality imaging suitable for most point-of-care applications, though it doesn't match the absolute performance of high-end cart systems costing 10-100x more. The semiconductor technology and AI optimization deliver clinically useful images for FAST exams, cardiac assessments, vascular access, and routine diagnostic scanning. For specialized applications requiring maximum resolution or deep penetration, traditional systems may be preferred, but for 80% of clinical ultrasound use cases, Butterfly iQ provides excellent diagnostic quality.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Do I need the subscription or can I use just the device?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">The device works without a subscription for basic imaging and local storage on your smartphone or tablet. However, the $49/month subscription unlocks crucial features including cloud storage, AI-powered measurements, telemedicine capabilities, advanced imaging modes, and continuous software updates. Most users find the subscription essential for professional use, especially for cloud archiving and AI assistance. The annual plan at $420/year saves 30% compared to monthly billing.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What devices are compatible with Butterfly iQ?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Butterfly iQ connects via USB-C to compatible iOS and Android devices. For iOS, it requires iPhone 8 or newer and iPad (5th generation or newer) running iOS 13 or later. For Android, it requires devices with USB-C ports running Android 9 or newer. The Butterfly iQ app is free to download. The device includes an adapter for older Lightning port iPhones. Check the Butterfly Network website for the most current compatibility list.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can Butterfly iQ integrate with our EHR system?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Butterfly iQ supports DICOM export and integrates with major EHR systems including Epic, Cerner, and others. Images can be exported directly to PACS systems or sent via secure links. Enterprise customers receive dedicated integration support and custom workflows. The cloud platform also provides APIs for custom integrations. All data transmission is HIPAA-compliant with end-to-end encryption.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is training required to use Butterfly iQ effectively?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">While physicians with ultrasound experience can start using Butterfly iQ immediately, the platform includes built-in training modules and scanning protocols for learning. The AI guidance helps users position the probe correctly and optimize images in real-time, significantly reducing the learning curve. Butterfly Network also offers online courses, webinars, and certification programs. Many users without prior ultrasound experience successfully learn basic point-of-care scanning within days, though mastery of advanced techniques requires practice and education like any diagnostic modality.</div></div>
